{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Automatic double tracking for vocals and other sources: four pitch-shifted, delayed copies spread across the stereo field, with high- and low-pass filters and separate dry and wet levels, ported from ADT by Christopher Arndt https://github.com/SpotlightKid/adt (MIT) JSFX version released under MIT license Claude Opus 5.x may have generated some of the port of this code\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Rotary speaker (Leslie) with horn and drum rotors, speed switching, brake, filters and cabinet geometry, ported from setBfree's b_whirl by Fredrik Kilander, Robin Gareus, Ken Restivo and Will Panther https://github.com/pantherb/setBfree (GPLv2+) JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license Claude generated some of this code\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 TR-909 style drum machine: circuit-modelled kick, snare, toms, rim shot and hand clap, sampled hi-hats, ride and crash, per-voice drive, distortion, pan and reverb/delay sends, master distortion and glue compressor, stereo or 11-channel multi-out (one output per voice as on the TR-909's back panel, hi-hats shared, plus an FX return; pan, master distortion and compressor are stereo only), ported from 9W9 by athousanddetails, after ER-99 by Matthew Cieplak https://github.com/athousanddetails/schwung-9W9 (GPLv3) JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license Claude generated some of this code\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Acoustic drum kit based on the AVL Drumkits Blonde Bop, played with sticks or Hot Rods (from Blonde Bop HR), 27 pieces on the GM drum map (notes 35-61, stick click on 35), 135 samples per set with five velocity layers, hi-hat and cymbal chokes, clickable kit photo, stereo or multi-channel (kick, snare, hi-hat, tom, floor tom, overheads, percussion) outputs, ported from avldrums.lv2 by Robin Gareus (fluidsynth sample engine, kit photo and hit map) https://github.com/x42/avldrums.lv2 (GPLv2+) Samples and kit photo: AVL Drumkits (Blonde Bop) by Glen MacArthur, http://www.bandshed.net/avldrumkits/ Samples as modified for avldrums.lv2, then reduced to 12-bit and joined into one file per set for this plugin; the sample files remain under CC-BY-SA 3.0 (see Dependencies/Drumkits/Goldibops-LICENSE.txt), and music made with it can be licensed freely JSFX code released under GPLv3+ license Claude Opus 5.x may have generated some of the port of this code\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
