{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Juno-style chorus with modes I, I+II and II, tone and mix controls, ported from junologue-chorus by Peter Allwin https://github.com/peterall/junologue-chorus (MIT) JSFX version released under MIT license Claude Opus 5.x may have generated some of the port of this code\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Taiko drums: S. Christian Collins' SCC Taiko Drums played through a port of the sfizz SFZ engine. Fifteen drums and hits on key pairs from C2 to A#4 (white key + the black key above it, for easy rolls), with velocity layers and round robins; how long a key is held sets how long the drum rings (hold the sustain pedal for full decays). Click a drum in the list to hear it. Ported from sfizz 1.2.3 (sfizz authors, https://sfz.tools/sfizz, BSD 2-clause). Samples: SCC Taiko Drums 1.0 by S. Christian Collins (https://www.schristiancollins.com), mostly from Subaqueous' Free Taiko Drum Rack (http://subaqueousmusic.com), CC BY-SA 4.0, with a freesound.org sample by whatsanickname4u (CC BY 3.0); joined into one 16-bit FLAC, released under CC BY-SA 4.0 (Dependencies/Kaminari/Kaminari-LICENSE.txt). JSFX code released under GPLv3+ license Claude generated some of this code\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Acoustic drum kit based on the AVL Drumkits Red Zeppelin 4-piece, 26 pieces on the GM drum map (notes 36-61), 118 samples with five velocity layers, hi-hat and cymbal chokes, clickable kit photo, stereo or multi-channel (kick, snare, hi-hat, tom, floor tom, overheads, percussion) outputs, ported from avldrums.lv2 by Robin Gareus (fluidsynth sample engine, kit photo and hit map) https://github.com/x42/avldrums.lv2 (GPLv2+) Samples and kit photo: AVL Drumkits (Red Zeppelin) by Glen MacArthur, http://www.bandshed.net/avldrumkits/ Samples as modified for avldrums.lv2, then reduced to 12-bit and joined into one file for this plugin; the sample file remains under CC-BY-SA 3.0 (see Dependencies/Drumkits/LedHead-LICENSE.txt), and music made with it can be licensed freely JSFX code released under GPLv3+ license Claude Opus 5.x may have generated some of the port of this code\par}
}

